Nivel de vechime: Nu se aplică
Tip de angajare: Full-time
Sectoare de activitate: Transport cu camionul și Fabricația de echipamente de cale ferată
At Alstom, we build what millions depend on daily - rail transportation systems that can't afford to fail. We're more than 85,000 people worldwide creating the industry's most diverse portfolio: high-speed trains, metros, trams, maintenance services and integrated systems.
 More Than a Job: A Mission 
 We are looking for a Senior Business Data Analyst to transform complex data into accurate, actionable insights that support strategic decision-making. You will collaborate with regions and key stakeholders to structure and consolidate data, identify trends, and leverage Power BI, Excel and AI-driven solutions to enhance data management and business performance.
 Your Role, Your Impact 
 Ensure the accuracy for the data gathering from region, sites and extraction from system; 
 Provide the reports/ data needed to make decisions to central team; 
 Support the sponsors and the regions with understanding the data or trends to drive the demand; 
Secure and define the data structuration in order to provide right efficiency to the process;
Compile and consolidate relevant data information coming from core team;
Structure the data extracted from the ERPs systems in an Excel sheet.
 You'll work with dedicated, proactive teams to turn complex data into meaningful insights, supporting informed decisions and business performance across the organization.
 What You Bring
 Degree level qualification; 
 Power BI expert / expert in Excel and in data management - preferably with Finance, Procurement, Projects backgrounds; 
 Good in PowerPoint and lead presentations for top management; 
 Can understand, explain, and interpret data; 
 Can drive governance with top management / different region heads / métiers; 
 Strong data crunching and data visualization skills, automation mindset, interested in information technologies and the usage of tools; 
 AI knowledge is a must, with the ability to apply AI to business intelligence, data analysis and insight generation; 
 Able to set up agentic behaviors and orchestrate AI workflows, including goals, tools, guardrails, hand-offs and human oversight; 
 Understands responsible AI, data security and the validation of AI-generated outputs against trusted business data; 
 Good knowledge of indirect procurement and pricing management; 
 Fluency in English, any other language is an advantage; 
 Structured and organized; 
 Agile mind set; 
 Collaboration & communication skills. 
 How Success Is Measured
 Accurate and timely data gathering, consolidation and reporting that supports informed business decisions; 
 Effective support to sponsors, regional teams and senior management in understanding data, trends and business insights; 
 Continuous improvement in data structuring, efficiency and automation, including the effective and responsible use of AI. 
 Alstom, A Great Place to Grow 
 Contribute to sustainable mobility projects with global impact from Cluj-Napoca; 
 Grow your career through continuous learning and development programs; 
 Perks and Benefits: 
 Enjoy stability, challenges and a long-term career free from boring daily routines; 
 Be part of a large team with over 1000 professionals in HR, Finance and Procurement & Supply Chain; 
 Collaborate with transverse teams and helpful colleagues; 
 Utilise our Agile, Responsible and Inclusive working environment; 
 Steer your career in whatever direction you choose across functions and countries; 
 Benefit from our investment in your development, through award-winning learning (Access to Alstom University and Alstom Learning Program); 
 Professional Development Plan – we offer great opportunities to develop yourself within the company; 
 Benefit from a fair and dynamic reward package that recognises your performance and potential (Competitive Salary and Meal Vouchers, Flexible Benefits at your choice - on top of your salary, Holiday Bonuses (Easter, Christmas), Employee Loyalty Bonus, Reimbursement of telework expenses – for amount of days worked from home, Additional Bonuses - referral bonuses, new-born bonus, discounts); 
 Entitle to comprehensive and competitive social coverage (Life and Accident Insurance, Private medical subscription at Regina Maria and Private Pension); 
 Work-life balance - we offer flexible working hours and a hybrid model of work (Working from Home 3 days/week) and 25 days of annual leave; 
 Be part of our Social Corporate Responsibilities initiatives (Social events, Humanitarian Actions). 
 Important to note 
 As a global business, we’re an equal-opportunity employer that celebrates diversity across the 70+ countries we operate in. We’re committed to creating an inclusive workplace for everyone.
